WEBVTT

00:00:02.170 --> 00:00:04.690
The three separated at a fork in the road.

00:00:05.220 --> 00:00:08.150
And now their whereabouts are undisclosed, do they want to protect themselves or other people.

00:00:08.150 --> 00:00:09.900
Or heavenly dreams?

00:00:10.520 --> 00:00:12.820
The creases of disorder are a cauldron of three.

00:00:13.560 --> 00:00:15.450
To an endless, eternal picture of Hell,

00:00:16.310 --> 00:00:19.580
pushing through time a door is dispelled.

00:00:20.190 --> 00:00:24.860
Your grudge shall be released.

00:00:37.400 --> 00:00:38.770
Who are you?

00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:40.950
Jigoku Shoujo.

00:00:41.380 --> 00:00:42.480
Didn’t you call me?

00:00:42.940 --> 00:00:44.740
You are?

00:00:44.740 --> 00:00:45.690
Yes.

00:00:46.380 --> 00:00:47.690
Yama-waro.

00:00:50.010 --> 00:00:51.050
Hikaru?

00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:52.940
Yes, Ojou.

00:00:57.220 --> 00:00:58.990
Take this.

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:40.170
This program is made possible by Sony Music, Aniplex,

00:02:40.170 --> 00:02:43.970
and the listed sponsors.

00:02:44.570 --> 00:02:48.360
We’ve known the Ashiya family since my father’s generation.

00:02:48.360 --> 00:02:51.890
Wait, maybe since my grandfather’s.

00:02:51.890 --> 00:02:54.520
So the couple is really…?

00:02:54.520 --> 00:02:56.070
Eighty or ninety.

00:02:56.070 --> 00:02:58.930
They might be over one hundred.

00:02:58.930 --> 00:02:59.870
One hundred?

00:03:00.350 --> 00:03:03.280
But I don’t think they want insurance.

00:03:03.280 --> 00:03:04.650
Why?

00:03:04.700 --> 00:03:06.940
They don’t have any children or grandchildren.

00:03:06.940 --> 00:03:10.640
Actually, they had children, but I heard they died.

00:03:10.640 --> 00:03:11.970
When was this?

00:03:12.900 --> 00:03:14.580
Before the war.

00:03:14.580 --> 00:03:18.400
It was after that when they disassociated from the world.

00:03:22.580 --> 00:03:26.950
Biologist Ashiya Risaburo’s eldest son, Hikaru’s whereabouts

00:03:26.950 --> 00:03:31.680
is, even with the Police and Fire Department’s desperate search efforts, still unknown.

00:03:31.680 --> 00:03:33.890
At last the search has been confirmed to end.

00:03:33.890 --> 00:03:36.550
It appears he probably sank in the swamp.

00:03:36.550 --> 00:03:39.570
In the past, sinking to the bottom of the swamps in this area…

00:03:41.870 --> 00:03:43.840
When did this happened?

00:03:43.840 --> 00:03:48.410
During elementary school… Maybe around the time of the Osaka World Expo.

00:03:48.900 --> 00:03:52.580
In the forest, I was looking for insects and got lost.

00:03:53.460 --> 00:03:58.900
Then a boy about the same age appeared,
and lead me to the exit.

00:03:58.900 --> 00:03:59.960
Oh.

00:04:00.400 --> 00:04:03.730
As I didn’t know him, I asked where his house was.

00:04:03.730 --> 00:04:06.970
And he pointed at that mansion and said “there”.

00:04:07.210 --> 00:04:11.600
When I went home and talked about it, they told me that the boy doesn’t exist.

00:04:12.510 --> 00:04:15.010
I was really scared.

00:04:15.010 --> 00:04:16.430
As would be expected.

00:04:18.400 --> 00:04:19.820
We have a job.

00:04:20.310 --> 00:04:22.660
The client’s name is Ashiya Fujiko.

00:04:24.190 --> 00:04:25.050
Then I’ll-

00:04:25.500 --> 00:04:27.140
Give that job to me!

00:04:27.140 --> 00:04:28.200
Eh?

00:04:29.440 --> 00:04:31.350
I don’t mind.

00:04:31.790 --> 00:04:33.900
What’s your reason? It depends on that.

00:04:34.520 --> 00:04:35.960
The reason is that…

00:04:36.760 --> 00:04:41.460
To quickly become like you all, I thought I needed more experience.

00:04:41.810 --> 00:04:44.910
Oh, how admirable.

00:04:44.910 --> 00:04:46.470
N-Not really.

00:04:47.260 --> 00:04:49.790
Being such a suck-up. Face me!

00:04:49.810 --> 00:04:51.210
Yes, hime.

00:04:54.820 --> 00:04:55.980
Is it OK?

00:04:57.500 --> 00:04:58.550
Sure.

00:04:58.550 --> 00:04:59.990
Thank you very much!

00:05:01.620 --> 00:05:03.330
It’s twisted.

00:05:41.840 --> 00:05:44.590
I’m very sorry for intruding so suddenly.

00:05:44.590 --> 00:05:47.320
My name is Mikage Yuzuki.

00:05:48.310 --> 00:05:53.590
In truth, I would like to speak to your household’s grandma… no, grandmother.

00:05:54.250 --> 00:05:55.600
Grandmother?

00:05:55.600 --> 00:05:57.890
Yes, about eighty years old.

00:05:57.890 --> 00:05:59.570
There’s no one like that.

00:06:01.880 --> 00:06:05.470
The only ones in this house are only my wife and I.

00:06:05.690 --> 00:06:08.170
Oh, honey, where’s Hikaru?

00:06:08.170 --> 00:06:11.670
Oh, right, and Hikaru.

00:06:11.670 --> 00:06:15.070
He’s our son. A boy.

00:06:15.820 --> 00:06:16.930
Oh.

00:06:23.710 --> 00:06:26.040
Is something wrong? Maybe you’re sick?

00:06:26.300 --> 00:06:28.430
Oh no, I’m fine!

00:06:28.430 --> 00:06:31.670
Seems like I’ve mistaken houses. I’m sorry.

00:06:34.930 --> 00:06:37.760
Something’s strange. Something…

00:06:42.280 --> 00:06:44.100
I wonder what that was…

00:06:44.100 --> 00:06:45.260
Dunno.

00:06:48.290 --> 00:06:49.510
Oh!

00:06:52.550 --> 00:06:53.770
Who are you?

00:06:53.770 --> 00:06:54.850
Kikuri.

00:06:54.920 --> 00:06:57.180
Did you come with that person just now?

00:06:57.180 --> 00:06:58.110
No.

00:06:58.580 --> 00:07:01.260
Then, Hikaru’s friend?

00:07:01.440 --> 00:07:03.510
You came to play, didn’t you?

00:07:03.510 --> 00:07:04.810
Thank you!

00:07:14.600 --> 00:07:16.500
Hikaru! It’s your mother!

00:07:16.500 --> 00:07:17.910
I’m coming in.

00:07:18.400 --> 00:07:22.370
Hikaru, your friend came to play!

00:07:23.540 --> 00:07:24.760
Kikuri-chan.

00:07:27.480 --> 00:07:28.700
Really!

00:07:29.480 --> 00:07:30.940
How lucky!

00:07:31.560 --> 00:07:34.180
Your mother has to prepare dinner,

00:07:34.800 --> 00:07:36.700
so Kikuri-chan, you should eat here too!

00:07:39.650 --> 00:07:41.850
What are you doing, Waro-waro?

00:07:41.850 --> 00:07:42.710
I’m sleeping.

00:07:42.710 --> 00:07:44.310
I can see that.

00:07:44.640 --> 00:07:49.960
That woman, does she not know the difference between her own child and a straw doll?

00:07:49.960 --> 00:07:52.600
No, I, a long time ago…

00:07:53.910 --> 00:07:56.010
…was that person’s child.

00:07:56.010 --> 00:07:57.680
What is that?

00:07:58.340 --> 00:08:00.850
Can you see the mountains outside of the window?

00:08:02.990 --> 00:08:06.260
I was born in those mountains.

00:08:08.270 --> 00:08:10.790
Ever since I was born, I was alone.

00:08:11.370 --> 00:08:13.940
No parents, no companions.

00:08:15.190 --> 00:08:17.930
Occasionally some people stepped foot in the mountains.

00:08:21.480 --> 00:08:23.900
But when they saw me…

00:08:27.950 --> 00:08:29.280
It was then,

00:08:29.730 --> 00:08:31.480
when I met Ojou.

00:08:34.430 --> 00:08:36.160
<i>Would you like to come with me?</i>

00:08:36.160 --> 00:08:37.970
<i>Are you not lonely?</i>

00:08:37.970 --> 00:08:38.970
<i>What?</i>

00:08:39.860 --> 00:08:42.230
<i>Always alone.</i>

00:08:42.230 --> 00:08:43.210
<i>Not really.</i>

00:08:44.090 --> 00:08:46.640
<i>If you change your mind, come by any time.</i>

00:08:50.010 --> 00:08:52.210
I wasn’t toughening it out.

00:08:52.850 --> 00:08:56.520
I thought being alone was normal.

00:09:08.320 --> 00:09:12.710
That was the first time I saw a human family.

00:09:12.710 --> 00:09:14.490
Why they were laughing,

00:09:14.860 --> 00:09:18.100
myself at that time could not understand.

00:09:18.100 --> 00:09:18.940
That…

00:09:19.480 --> 00:09:21.950
<i>Hikaru!</i>

00:09:37.070 --> 00:09:39.380
It was curiosity at first.

00:09:49.640 --> 00:09:55.760
It’s almost complete. Ambrosia, which gives eternal life.

00:10:17.920 --> 00:10:19.450
Just a bit longer.

00:10:19.450 --> 00:10:22.310
After that, a long time passed.

00:10:37.830 --> 00:10:40.050
<i>What is that?</i>

00:10:40.730 --> 00:10:43.860
<i>It’s Caterpillar fungus that I selectively bred.</i>

00:10:44.370 --> 00:10:45.920
<i>Now, drink it.</i>

00:10:52.440 --> 00:10:53.500
<i>How is it?</i>

00:10:54.740 --> 00:10:56.870
<i>I feel a bit better.</i>

00:10:57.850 --> 00:10:59.150
<i>I see.</i>

00:11:09.900 --> 00:11:11.080
<i>Hikaru,</i>

00:11:11.830 --> 00:11:14.180
<i>your mother will join you soon.</i>

00:11:20.370 --> 00:11:22.630
<i>Mother?</i>

00:11:23.740 --> 00:11:28.370
Why I did such a thing, I didn’t understand much myself.

00:11:28.370 --> 00:11:29.770
Probably,

00:11:29.770 --> 00:11:32.870
before she died, I wanted to show her a dream.

00:11:33.510 --> 00:11:34.960
<i>Hikaru!</i>

00:11:35.240 --> 00:11:36.220
<i>Hikaru!</i>

00:11:37.040 --> 00:11:37.970
<i>Hikaru!</i>

00:11:39.300 --> 00:11:43.220
That was the first time I touched someone.

00:11:44.730 --> 00:11:46.470
<i>Mother.</i>

00:11:49.960 --> 00:11:50.980
<i>That child!</i>

00:11:52.330 --> 00:11:54.570
<i>What are you saying, honey?</i>

00:11:54.570 --> 00:11:55.620
<i>It’s Hikaru!</i>

00:11:55.620 --> 00:11:57.830
<i>Hikaru came back!</i>

00:12:14.120 --> 00:12:17.400
<i>I’m glad the size is perfect!</i>

00:12:17.490 --> 00:12:19.680
<i>Hikaru, how about a “thank you” to your mother?</i>

00:12:20.640 --> 00:12:21.920
<i>Yes.</i>

00:12:21.920 --> 00:12:23.500
<i>Thank you, mother.</i>

00:12:33.410 --> 00:12:37.910
I began feeling as if I was really a member of that family.

00:12:42.690 --> 00:12:44.990
<i>Where are you from?</i>

00:12:45.950 --> 00:12:46.990
<i>Over there.</i>

00:12:51.740 --> 00:12:53.710
<i>Goodbye!</i>

00:12:55.840 --> 00:12:59.740
<i>It would be better to avoid contacting city people.</i>

00:13:00.430 --> 00:13:03.730
<i>Those are the rules of people who are not human.</i>

00:13:04.730 --> 00:13:07.500
<i>Then you, knowing that…</i>

00:13:07.500 --> 00:13:08.720
<i>Why?</i>

00:13:09.380 --> 00:13:10.720
<i>Come with me.</i>

00:13:18.010 --> 00:13:20.380
<i>Called Caterpillar fungus,</i>

00:13:20.380 --> 00:13:24.110
<i>it lives as a parasite in insects like moths or ants.</i>

00:13:24.770 --> 00:13:30.750
<i>Used to be an insect in the winter,  becomes grass in the summer, which explains it’s name.</i>

00:13:30.750 --> 00:13:33.120
<i>It is also an ingredient in traditional Chinese medicine.</i>

00:13:33.120 --> 00:13:35.520
<i>What would happen if Caterpillar fungus is used as a parasite</i>

00:13:35.520 --> 00:13:38.200
<i>in an organism other than an insect has been my long-held research topic.</i>

00:13:38.200 --> 00:13:40.660
<i>I tried many things,</i>

00:13:41.440 --> 00:13:45.600
<i>but I was unable to produce the results I wanted.</i>

00:13:46.380 --> 00:13:48.950
<i>And there I have a favor to ask of you.</i>

00:13:49.860 --> 00:13:50.880
<i>What is it?</i>

00:13:52.560 --> 00:13:55.360
<i>Can I use it as a parasite on you?</i>

00:13:57.000 --> 00:13:59.370
<i>If it’s scientifically impossible,</i>

00:13:59.370 --> 00:14:05.240
<i>you unscientific beings might be able to produce success.</i>

00:14:07.330 --> 00:14:10.680
<i>I beg of you. I want to save my wife!</i>

00:14:11.890 --> 00:14:17.770
<i>My wife’s life is not much longer. Unlike you, human death is inevitable,</i>

00:14:17.770 --> 00:14:22.330
<i>but I want to make my wife’s life even a little bit longer.</i>

00:14:22.930 --> 00:14:24.080
<i>What do you think?</i>

00:14:25.010 --> 00:14:29.030
I felt bad for the organisms called “humans”.

00:14:29.030 --> 00:14:32.990
Holding onto the past to escape from suffering.

00:14:32.990 --> 00:14:35.880
Chasing dreams that will never be granted.

00:14:37.160 --> 00:14:38.230
And so…

00:14:39.640 --> 00:14:41.170
<i>I understand.</i>

00:14:41.170 --> 00:14:42.940
<i>If you’re OK with me.</i>

00:14:49.660 --> 00:14:54.540
<i>Filatrix flemortum un colum colum vili.</i>

00:14:54.540 --> 00:14:55.100
<i>What?</i>

00:14:57.090 --> 00:14:59.040
<i>It’s an incantation that makes the medicine work.</i>

00:15:05.510 --> 00:15:06.890
<i>Are you OK?</i>

00:15:07.420 --> 00:15:08.400
<i>Yes.</i>

00:15:44.080 --> 00:15:45.370
<i>How is it?</i>

00:15:46.540 --> 00:15:50.520
<i>My head whirls a bit. Is there any alcohol in it?</i>

00:15:50.520 --> 00:15:51.010
<i>Yes.</i>

00:15:52.620 --> 00:15:54.510
<i>But it seems like it’s good for my body.</i>

00:15:57.140 --> 00:16:02.460
But, the effect of that medicine was stronger than anyone imagined.

00:16:06.670 --> 00:16:08.020
Hikaru.

00:16:08.020 --> 00:16:08.730
I refuse!

00:16:09.200 --> 00:16:10.420
What do you mean, “I refuse”?

00:16:10.420 --> 00:16:12.920
Lies! People don’t get younger!

00:16:12.920 --> 00:16:15.230
But you saw that person just now, right?

00:16:15.230 --> 00:16:16.450
Show me proof!

00:16:16.800 --> 00:16:19.730
Then examine my body!

00:16:19.730 --> 00:16:21.120
Well then…

00:16:23.650 --> 00:16:25.340
Whoa! What is this?!

00:16:25.340 --> 00:16:27.180
It’s Caterpillar Fungus.

00:16:27.180 --> 00:16:28.840
Do you believe me now?

00:16:30.610 --> 00:16:31.390
Let’s take it out!

00:16:31.390 --> 00:16:33.630
Don’t touch it! It’ll be a parasite on you!

00:16:34.870 --> 00:16:38.600
I don’t know for sure, but that danger is plenty.

00:16:38.790 --> 00:16:39.790
Let’s run away!

00:16:39.790 --> 00:16:40.630
No.

00:16:40.630 --> 00:16:41.580
I order you!

00:16:41.580 --> 00:16:43.220
Even if it’s hime’s orders, I can’t follow them.

00:16:43.220 --> 00:16:44.910
Why?!

00:16:45.600 --> 00:16:47.190
That person also,

00:16:47.190 --> 00:16:48.620
a long time ago…

00:16:50.320 --> 00:16:52.690
<i>Mother! Mother, where are we going!</i>

00:16:54.640 --> 00:16:56.170
<i>We’re going to run away, Hikaru.</i>

00:16:56.170 --> 00:16:56.900
<i>What?</i>

00:16:56.900 --> 00:17:01.070
<i>I saw what that person was doing with your body.</i>

00:17:01.070 --> 00:17:03.250
<i>If it’s about that, there’s no need to worry.</i>

00:17:03.440 --> 00:17:05.610
<i>That person said the same thing.</i>

00:17:05.610 --> 00:17:08.800
<i>No need to worry, because that child is not human.</i>

00:17:09.780 --> 00:17:13.920
<i>It’s OK, whether or not you’re human.</i>

00:17:13.920 --> 00:17:15.760
<i>You’re my child!</i>

00:17:16.270 --> 00:17:18.910
<i>But we can’t stay here.</i>

00:17:18.910 --> 00:17:20.910
<i>What will that person do to you?</i>

00:17:22.550 --> 00:17:25.360
<i>So please, run away!</i>

00:17:25.360 --> 00:17:26.620
<i>But…</i>

00:17:26.620 --> 00:17:27.620
<i>But!</i>

00:17:27.620 --> 00:17:30.770
<i>If I’m not here, mother.</i>

00:17:30.970 --> 00:17:32.370
<i>I know.</i>

00:17:33.250 --> 00:17:34.780
<i>But it’s for your sake!</i>

00:17:35.540 --> 00:17:36.580
<i>Stay healthy!</i>

00:17:37.200 --> 00:17:38.180
<i>Hikaru…</i>

00:17:40.660 --> 00:17:41.850
<i>Go!</i>

00:17:45.110 --> 00:17:46.240
<i>Quickly!</i>

00:17:51.610 --> 00:17:53.070
It was then…

00:17:53.540 --> 00:17:55.470
The pain of saying farewell,

00:17:55.470 --> 00:17:56.930
I understood it.

00:17:59.390 --> 00:18:01.480
I thought we would never meet again.

00:18:01.480 --> 00:18:03.690
And then this happens.

00:18:03.690 --> 00:18:07.440
I know that since she’s human, her life will inevitably end.

00:18:08.280 --> 00:18:11.230
But, dying and being sent to Hell…

00:18:11.230 --> 00:18:13.600
Are you going to stop it? The ferrying?

00:18:13.820 --> 00:18:16.320
No, I have no plan of doing so.

00:18:17.340 --> 00:18:20.450
If my string is pulled, I’ll…

00:18:20.450 --> 00:18:22.400
I don’t understand!

00:18:22.400 --> 00:18:24.330
Even I don’t understand!

00:18:24.330 --> 00:18:25.460
Hikaru!

00:18:25.920 --> 00:18:28.360
I brought some dinner.

00:18:30.440 --> 00:18:32.340
Thank you, mother.

00:18:33.240 --> 00:18:37.140
Oh, what happened? Sweating that much.

00:18:44.300 --> 00:18:46.030
Waro-waro is not Hikaru!

00:18:46.030 --> 00:18:47.730
W-What is this?

00:18:47.730 --> 00:18:51.190
Because you ask the Hell Correspondence, Waro-waro is in trouble!

00:18:51.770 --> 00:18:53.430
Hell Correspondence?

00:18:53.430 --> 00:18:55.070
Didn’t you request it?

00:18:59.370 --> 00:19:00.500
That person…

00:19:01.260 --> 00:19:02.700
That person, to Hikaru…

00:19:06.290 --> 00:19:08.250
Send that person to Hell!

00:19:14.180 --> 00:19:15.750
Hikaru’s vengeance!

00:19:16.880 --> 00:19:17.880
Lies.

00:19:17.880 --> 00:19:22.270
I haven’t killed Hikaru, nor have I used him in human experiments.

00:19:23.110 --> 00:19:24.890
That was an accident.

00:19:25.280 --> 00:19:27.270
What a sad accident.

00:19:27.390 --> 00:19:28.790
Then why?!

00:19:29.140 --> 00:19:31.870
I needed someone that was not human…

00:19:32.380 --> 00:19:34.790
…for the research of eternal life.

00:19:35.880 --> 00:19:38.100
For my research.

00:19:38.450 --> 00:19:41.320
You tricked him in order for you to create that medicine!

00:19:42.040 --> 00:19:43.950
But I wonder why?

00:19:43.950 --> 00:19:46.720
Caterpillar fungus was growing on him…

00:19:47.360 --> 00:19:49.760
Well, I’m glad I was saved the effort.

00:20:01.640 --> 00:20:03.060
Let’s make a toast!

00:20:03.060 --> 00:20:06.600
While we have this Ambrosia, we are eternal.

00:20:07.140 --> 00:20:10.770
As long as Hikaru lived, I could’ve given you it.

00:20:12.280 --> 00:20:14.580
What do you think, Hikaru?

00:20:14.940 --> 00:20:17.800
No! Don’t pull the string!

00:20:20.120 --> 00:20:23.030
Of course. You’re sick of it, right?

00:20:23.690 --> 00:20:26.510
Let’s make him stop. Together.

00:20:29.570 --> 00:20:32.750
Your grudge is received.

00:20:44.330 --> 00:20:46.330
Waro-waro, face me!

00:20:46.550 --> 00:20:48.100
Yes, hime.

00:20:48.210 --> 00:20:49.720
What are you doing?

00:20:49.810 --> 00:20:52.360
Waro-waro said he doesn’t want to punish.

00:20:52.980 --> 00:20:56.790
Don’t you have a lot of grudges, too? Then greasily-

00:20:56.790 --> 00:20:58.220
I refuse, hime.

00:20:58.220 --> 00:21:00.730
I have no grudges.

00:21:00.730 --> 00:21:02.640
Don’t talk back at me!

00:21:02.640 --> 00:21:03.640
Why?

00:21:04.460 --> 00:21:07.370
Because I’m not human.

00:21:07.810 --> 00:21:09.120
Oh.

00:21:11.530 --> 00:21:14.310
More importantly, I’m worried about her.

00:21:14.310 --> 00:21:15.680
Can I go?

00:21:16.830 --> 00:21:17.940
Sure.

00:21:33.050 --> 00:21:34.210
It can’t be!

00:22:10.010 --> 00:22:14.170
<i>I sincerely think humans are sad living beings.</i>

00:22:14.170 --> 00:22:16.610
<i>Why they do such things?</i>

00:22:16.610 --> 00:22:19.630
<i>I sometimes distressed by trying to understand.</i>

00:22:19.630 --> 00:22:23.960
<i>After starting the job with Hell Correspondence, I especially think so.</i>

00:22:23.950 --> 00:22:27.850
<i>But, to mountains without any people like a long time ago,</i>

00:22:27.850 --> 00:22:29.490
<i>I don’t think I’ll return.</i>

00:22:30.420 --> 00:22:32.730
<i>Being alone is lonely after all.</i>

00:22:34.920 --> 00:22:37.690
<i>As long as this continues to live inside of me.</i>

00:22:38.440 --> 00:22:40.230
<i>You…</i>

00:22:40.230 --> 00:22:42.210
<i>I will never forget…</i>

00:22:44.960 --> 00:22:49.970
Note: Candle says,  Ashiya Fujiko.

00:22:47.510 --> 00:22:49.120
<i>…mother.</i>

00:24:21.390 --> 00:24:22.360
Your name?

00:24:22.360 --> 00:24:23.870
Hamano Chiriko.

00:24:23.870 --> 00:24:27.690
Is that radio show that interesting?

00:24:27.690 --> 00:24:30.080
Chotaro changed me.

00:24:30.080 --> 00:24:33.270
With Cinderella’s magic I changed!

00:24:34.110 --> 00:24:35.440
Chotaro is amazing.

00:24:36.330 --> 00:24:38.680
Which is why… please…

00:24:39.010 --> 00:24:40.750
…send them to Hell.

00:24:41.310 --> 00:24:44.460
Your grudge is received.

00:24:44.790 --> 00:24:47.940
Next time: Special Radio.

00:24:50.710 --> 00:24:55.880
